"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Cold Heart Heretic (Blazing Soul Priest), Lord of Sablak</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_overflow-x-auto_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Minor Exalted</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Unfettered Youth</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">The last (probably) Nocturnal, whose attempts to free the imprisoned Nocturnal shards created the fault lines in Creation that allow Gem to be attack</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Release the Nocturnals</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Berit, (Misrak, Jamila, Gadise, Enku, Hamrawi)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_overflow-x-auto_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Neirites</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Priest Samson's illegitmate son from a pilgrimage years ago, is now Unfettered Youth's sole assistant in releasing the Nocturnals</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Help Unfettered Youth/Find a way back into his family.</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">(Misrak, Jamila, Gadise, Enku, Hamrawi), Singing Crow</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_overflow-x-auto_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Kokebe of Werku</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Zenebe of Werku's neice and heir, now a Hearteater trying to take over the local Guild Office</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Take over Gem's Guild Office</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Zenebe of Werku</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_overflow-x-auto_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Ulko Demise</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">A recent Breath Liminal, is trying to figure out why the ghosts seem to be fewer recently</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Investigate Gem's Ghosts</td> <td class=\"text_table_align-left text_table_overflow-x-auto_td\">Hunter</td> </tr> </table></div> This might be too much, but I won't flesh them out unless the players start looking into that character's specific direction.<br /> <br /> And a few closing remarks:<ul><li>Hergal is based of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1554750-idea-for-a-central-bank-in-yu-shan-six-dragon-and-nine-minister-bank\">this concept I had for a central bank of Yu Shan</a>. Golden Voice that Silences All is Zaskal of the Smiles as a Deathlord.</li> <li>The ice vampires are a home brew species of Dark Brood that suck out the heat of targets to survive; they thrive under Gem by eat at magma vents, which cool down the whole of Mount Cinere centuries ago, leaving Gem as a caldera and not an active volcano. They're arrogant but largely peaceful. Might either be a fully prehuman race or tied to this Avatistic Exalted concept I had - basically humans infused with the essence of fallen races and able to mutate human followers based on their specific fallen race; in that case the Ice vampires would be the dwindling but immortal servants of a past Avatistic Exalt whose shard is being used as the final seal for the nocturnals. Is that a bit too much to add?</li> <li>I'm not sure about my concepts for the demons involved and I'm not sure if there are any better fits. Also not sure what to do with the Fair Folk but I'll give it a try with the concepts I have.</li> <li>Gem was attack but not destroyed; it's outer walls are broken in some places but work is being done to fix them and the Fair Folk, Demons and Undead and mostly outside. The Autochthonians are under ground and the various mortals, exalts and gods are based around the city.</li> <li>Is there anyone you think I should add and if so why?</li> <li>Any other thoughts an suggestions?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}